<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mustafa Kemal Atatürk</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mustafa Kemal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mustafa Kemal Atatürk was an Ottoman army officer who led the Turkish national movement after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> and became the founding president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-turkey">Republic of Turkey</a>. Following the Ottoman defeat and the Allied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/occupation-of-istanbul">occupation of Istanbul</a>, his forces resisted the post-war partition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. His success marked the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and its replacement by a secular national republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mustafa-kemal-ataturk.jpg" alt="Mustafa Kemal Atatürk" width="312" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ataturk1930s.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
